<%#
  Open Settings button + its warning banner (issues #992, #1005, #1024)

  The one definition of the way through to the iRaceDeck Settings window, used
  by every place that offers it: `action-settings-footer.ejs` (the 35 action
  PIs, where it closes the action's own settings) and `section-header.ejs` (the
  plugin-level `settings.ejs` page, where it sits under the heading).

  The banner above it carries the OPEN failure and only that: the window could
  not be displayed although the settings service is healthy. It stays HERE
  rather than in the page-top strip that `head-common.ejs` injects, so that a
  press that produces no window explains itself next to the button that was
  pressed. #1005 argued that from distance — the button was then at the very
  bottom of an action PI, a full scroll from the strip. #1024 moved it up near
  the top, so the distance argument is spent, but the placement is not: a
  warning about one control belongs beside that control, which is the general
  rule the `only`/`except` filters exist to serve.

  The SERVER failure deliberately stays in the top strip instead. It is not
  about this button: with no service a PI has no channel to the plugin, so
  every setting the page can change is inert, and that belongs where the page
  announces page-wide problems.

  `head-common.ejs` gives the top strip the matching `except`, so the open
  banner appears in exactly one place per page. The id literal is duplicated
  from deck-core's SETTINGS_WINDOW_OPEN_WARNING_ID (this bundle is browser code
  and cannot import it); `settings-window-constants.test.ts` guards the pair.

  Banner and button share ONE outer block, and `extraClass` goes on that block
  rather than on the button's own wrapper. `.ird-section-footer` draws the
  divider that closes a section with a `border-top`, so putting the banner
  outside the block would render it ABOVE that rule — reading as the tail of
  the settings above it, with a horizontal line between it and the button it
  explains. The button wrapper also centres its content, which is right for a
  button and wrong for a paragraph of warning text, so the banner stays a
  sibling of that wrapper rather than a child of it.

  Parameters:
    - extraClass (String, optional) — class list for the outer block.
    - size (String, optional) — "standard" for the full-width pill, on a page
      where this button is the only thing to press. Omit it among an action's
      own settings, where the component's own quiet default is what stops it
      outshouting the settings the panel is about (#1024).
%>
<div<% if (locals.extraClass) { %> class="<%= extraClass %>"<% } %>>
  <ird-warnings only="settings-window-open"></ird-warnings>
  <div class="ird-open-settings">
    <ird-open-settings<% if (locals.size) { %> size="<%= size %>"<% } %>></ird-open-settings>
  </div>
</div>
